Hi all,

I started an analysis with BioGeoBears, but I have one problem needing your help.

My study taxa is endemic to Southeast Asia and I partitioned it into three areas: Indo-Burma, Thai-Malay Peninsula and Borneo according the geographic and environmental features. In addition, the distribution range of the outgroup is similar with the whole range of my study taxa. I want to include the outgroup in the analysis but I do not know its origin.

In this situation, how do I deal with the outgroup? Is it necessary to exclude the outgroup to eliminate the bias in the analysis?

Thank you very much.

Best wishes.

Chen

